  "id": "revista_portuguesa",
  "name": "Revista à portuguesa (Lisbon Parque Mayer revue song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The revista à portuguesa is Lisbon's satirical musical revue, staged since the mid-nineteenth century and centred in the twentieth on the theatres of the Parque Mayer, where sketches of political and social satire alternated with songs, fados, marchas and dance numbers written for each season's show. Its songs, launched by the revue's stars with a small theatre orchestra, reached a wide public through records, radio and film. The credited-horns card stands for the orchestra's trumpet and other brass.",
  "recipe": "classic European mid-1960s revista à portuguesa, functional Song, iberian branch. one note per syllable, solo with instrumental accompaniment. upright piano, credited horns unspecified, clarinet, double bass, bronze bell bronze brushes-and-sticks drum kit. shoebox concert hall. Neumann U67, tube pre, colored vintage console, vari-mu, Pultec passive program EQ. tape 15ips echo plate reverb.",
